  "mn43:10.1": "",
  "mn43:10.2": "The import of this passage is that while one is in any of these three formless states, one can analyze them with discernment in a way that can lead to release. On the fact that this cannot be done with regard to the fourth formless state, see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn111'>MN 111</a>. On the fact that the external senses can fall silent while one is in these states, see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an9.37'>AN 9:37</a>.",
